          %title Dependent choice
          %h1#dependent_choice Dependent choice
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#statement"} Statement
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_set_theory"}  In set theory
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_a_topos_or_pretopos"} In a topos or pretopos
              %li
                %a{:href => "#applications"} Applications
              %li
                %a{:href => "#acceptability"} Acceptability
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#statement Statement
          %h3#in_set_theory  In set theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            %strong dependent choice
            (DC) states that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a nonempty (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"}> inhabited
            ) set and if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entire+relation"} total
            binary relation on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon \mathbb{N} \to X
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_n, x_{n+1})
            belongs to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+choice"} countable choice
            %em dependent
            choice because the available choices for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_{n+1}
            depend on the choice of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_n
            made at the previous stage.
          %p
            There is another way to express the axiom of dependent choice which uses
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjections"} surjections
            instead of entire relations:
          %p
            The
            %strong axiom of dependent choice
            states that given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+sets"} family of sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n
            and a family of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjections"} surjections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n:X_{n + 1} \to X_n
            indexed by natural numbers
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 2
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0 \overset{f_0}\leftarrow X_1 \overset{f_1}\leftarrow X_1 \overset{f_2}\leftarrow \ldots
          %p
            the projection function to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+limit"} sequential limit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ←
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\leftarrow}\lim X_n
            of the above diagram is a surjection.
          %h3#in_a_topos_or_pretopos In a topos or pretopos
          %p
            More generally, given an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
            or a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+limits"} sequential limits
            %strong axiom of dependent choice
            states that given a sequence of objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X:\mathbb{N} \to \mathrm{Ob}(\mathcal{E})
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sequence"} dependent sequence
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                    %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n:\mathrm{hom}_\mathcal{E}(X_{n + 1}, X_{n})
            indexed by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+limit"} sequential limit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ←
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\leftarrow}\lim X_n
            of the above diagram is an epimorphism.
          %h2#applications Applications
          %p
            Typical applications of dependent choice include
            %span.newWikiWord
              Kőnig's lemma
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/K%C5%91nig%27s+lemma"} ?
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baire+category+theorem"} Baire category theorem
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+metric+spaces"} complete metric spaces
          %h2#acceptability Acceptability
          %p
            The axiom of dependent choice holds in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+sets"} condensed sets
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+condensed+sets"} light condensed sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
          %p
            For a number of schools of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            of interest in which full AC doesn’t hold, including all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+toposes"} presheaf toposes
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+topos"} effective topos
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentation+axiom"} presentation axiom
          %p Like countable choice, it fails for sheaves over the space of real numbers.
